### Capstone Architecture: Employee Management & Payroll System

Our **Employee Management & Payroll System** orchestrates enterprise payroll distribution using comprehensive OOP principles:

```text
                         +-----------------------+
                         |       Payable         | (Interface)
                         +-----------------------+
                         | + calculatePay(): dbl |
                         +-----------------------+
                                     ^
                                     | implements
                         +-----------------------+
                         |       Employee        | (Abstract Class)
                         +-----------------------+
                         | - empId: String       |
                         | - name: String        |
                         +-----------------------+
                                     ^
               +---------------------+---------------------+
               |                                           |
+------------------------------+            +------------------------------+
|       SalariedEmployee       |            |        HourlyEmployee        |
+------------------------------+            +------------------------------+
| - monthlySalary: double      |            | - hourlyRate: double         |
| + calculatePay(): double     |            | - hoursWorked: double        |
+------------------------------+            | + calculatePay(): double     |
                                            +------------------------------+
```

**Architectural Highlights:**
1. **Contract Abstraction**: `Payable` interface enables polymorphic settlement across regular staff and third-party contractors.
2. **Encapsulated State**: Base fields are private, validated via constructor chaining.
3. **Polymorphic Payroll Processing**: The payroll orchestrator processes heterogeneous collections cleanly.

---

### Executable Capstone Implementation

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

interface Payable {
    double calculatePay();
}

abstract class Employee implements Payable {
    private final String empId;
    private final String name;

    public Employee(String empId, String name) {
        if (empId == null || name == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Fields cannot be null");
        this.empId = empId;
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getName() { return name; }
    public String getEmpId() { return empId; }
}

class SalariedEmployee extends Employee {
    private final double monthlySalary;

    public SalariedEmployee(String empId, String name, double monthlySalary) {
        super(empId, name);
        this.monthlySalary = monthlySalary;
    }

    @Override
    public double calculatePay() {
        return monthlySalary;
    }
}

class HourlyEmployee extends Employee {
    private final double hourlyRate;
    private final double hoursWorked;

    public HourlyEmployee(String empId, String name, double hourlyRate, double hoursWorked) {
        super(empId, name);
        this.hourlyRate = hourlyRate;
        this.hoursWorked = hoursWorked;
    }

    @Override
    public double calculatePay() {
        return hourlyRate * hoursWorked;
    }
}

public class PayrollSystemApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Payable> staff = new ArrayList<>();
        staff.add(new SalariedEmployee("EMP-01", "Marcus Vance", 8500.00));
        staff.add(new HourlyEmployee("EMP-02", "Elena Rostova", 45.00, 160));

        double totalDisbursement = 0.0;
        System.out.println("--- Monthly Payroll Disbursement ---");
        for (Payable p : staff) {
            double pay = p.calculatePay();
            totalDisbursement += pay;
            System.out.printf("Disbursed: $%.2f\n", pay);
        }
        System.out.printf("Total Payroll: $%.2f\n", totalDisbursement);
    }
}
```

**Console Output:**
```text
--- Monthly Payroll Disbursement ---
Disbursed: $8500.00
Disbursed: $7200.00
Total Payroll: $15700.00
```

